<title>CHINA: Parent in talks to sell HK Toy centre.</title>
<headline>Parent in talks to sell HK Toy centre.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toy maker Hong Kong Toy Centre International Ltd said on Friday its 74.7 percent controlling shareholder United Pacific Industries Ltd was in talks with third parties regarding sale of control of the company.</p>
<p>&quot;It has been approached over the past approximately two weeks by two parties,&quot; the company said in a statement. &quot;It is in preliminary negotiations on the possible sale of a controlling interest in Hong Kong Toy Centre.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said there was no certainty that any negotiations would be concluded satisfactorily.</p>
<p>Shares of Hong Kong Toy Centre eased HK$0.01 to HK$1.28 in late morning.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
